WEBVTT

00:01.459 --> 00:05.171
In the year 845, the Colossal Titan

00:05.255 --> 00:08.717
and the Armored Titan suddenly appeared.

00:09.259 --> 00:12.846
They destroyed one of humanity's walls
and everyday life with it.

00:14.514 --> 00:17.267
Humanity abandoned Wall Maria,

00:17.809 --> 00:20.979
lost twenty percent of its population
and one-third of its territory,

00:21.479 --> 00:25.108
and was forced to retreat
behind Wall Rose.

00:26.943 --> 00:29.821
And then, in the year 850...

00:30.780 --> 00:32.240
Humanity's fight back

00:33.158 --> 00:34.117
is just beginning!

00:37.162 --> 00:39.664
The target is the Colossal Titan
dead ahead!

00:40.874 --> 00:43.543
This is our chance! Don't let it get away!

00:46.671 --> 00:47.714
Hey there.

00:48.882 --> 00:50.300
It's been five years, hasn't it?

02:50.003 --> 02:53.131
He went for the cannons!

02:54.591 --> 02:57.093
And he didn't take out
the gate by accident, either!

02:58.469 --> 03:02.640
So he does have intelligence!

03:08.146 --> 03:09.606
Still, this is the perfect chance!

03:10.773 --> 03:12.859
He's the only one
who can destroy the wall!

03:15.278 --> 03:16.905
If I could just take him out...

03:24.621 --> 03:25.705
Too slow!

03:28.166 --> 03:29.167
Got you!

03:31.836 --> 03:32.837
What...

03:33.546 --> 03:34.756
Hot!

03:42.597 --> 03:46.142
Go!

03:50.104 --> 03:51.147
I missed?

03:57.028 --> 03:57.946
No.

03:58.821 --> 04:01.115
The Colossal Titan disappeared!

04:03.284 --> 04:05.787
Eren! Did you beat it?

04:06.287 --> 04:07.288
No!

04:08.331 --> 04:09.707
It's just like five years ago!

04:10.291 --> 04:13.336
He suddenly appeared,
then suddenly disappeared!

04:16.673 --> 04:18.424
I'm sorry. I let him get away.

04:18.716 --> 04:21.427
What are you apologizing for?
We were scared stiff--

04:21.511 --> 04:23.888
Hey! This is not the time for that!

04:24.305 --> 04:25.807
The wall has been broken!

04:26.140 --> 04:29.394
We have to hurry and seal it
before the Titans get in again!

04:29.769 --> 04:30.728
What are you doing?

04:31.271 --> 04:34.732
The Colossal Titan Response Operation
is already underway!

04:35.066 --> 04:36.192
Return to headquarters at once!

04:36.734 --> 04:39.362
Those who came into contact with it,
remember to give reports!

04:39.529 --> 04:42.365
- Yes, sir!
- We pray for the advance team's success!

04:58.965 --> 05:01.009
Take only absolute essentials!

05:01.342 --> 05:03.094
Please evacuate in a calm manner!

05:07.348 --> 05:08.766
If they break through here,

05:09.058 --> 05:12.103
we'll have another tragedy just like
five years ago on our hands!

05:13.146 --> 05:17.108
We must hold the Titans off here!

05:18.609 --> 05:19.902
Prepare to intercept!

05:22.488 --> 05:23.656
Fire!

05:30.288 --> 05:31.497
Charge!

05:35.293 --> 05:39.672
You cadets have successfully graduated!
You are now proper soldiers!

05:40.256 --> 05:42.508
I have high hopes for you
in this operation!

05:43.760 --> 05:45.178
Don't worry, Hanna.

05:46.220 --> 05:47.930
I promise I'll keep you safe.

05:48.306 --> 05:49.307
Franz.

05:53.019 --> 05:54.937
Are you okay, Armin?

05:55.396 --> 05:57.356
I'm fine!

05:57.774 --> 05:59.942
I'll calm down soon enough!

06:00.318 --> 06:01.819
Still, this is bad!

06:02.111 --> 06:06.574
We don't have the technology
to quickly seal an eight-meter-high hole!

06:07.325 --> 06:12.330
And we never did manage to unearth
that big rock near the front gate!

06:13.623 --> 06:17.502
Unless we seal the hole,
this city is as good as lost!

06:21.756 --> 06:25.343
It's only a matter of time
until Wall Rose is breached!

06:26.302 --> 06:29.305
In fact, if they ever feel like it,

06:29.472 --> 06:31.808
they can pretty much wipe out
humanity anytime they want!

06:32.141 --> 06:33.101
Armin!

06:33.768 --> 06:36.479
Calm down! This isn't like last time!

06:36.979 --> 06:39.941
Humanity won't lose
to any damn Titans this time!

06:44.987 --> 06:45.988
I'm sorry.

06:46.989 --> 06:48.074
I'm all right.

07:04.132 --> 07:07.301
Come on. Are you playing seriously?

07:08.302 --> 07:11.681
There. I win again.

07:12.807 --> 07:16.436
We square off once a month,

07:16.644 --> 07:20.356
yet you never seem
to improve at all, Pyxis.

07:20.523 --> 07:24.819
Oh, no, I am just no match
for you, Lord Wald.

07:29.323 --> 07:33.995
You're the top officer in charge
of the entire southern territory.

07:37.331 --> 07:39.584
How will you win against the Titans

07:39.750 --> 07:41.752
with such paltry skills and intellect?

07:41.836 --> 07:43.129
Commander Pyxis!

07:43.629 --> 07:44.630
I have a message!

07:45.047 --> 07:47.008
How uncouth! Who are you--

07:47.091 --> 07:49.594
The Colossal Titan has appeared in Trost!

07:50.136 --> 07:51.971
The gate has been destroyed!

08:06.110 --> 08:08.029
This is a fine wine, indeed.

08:08.696 --> 08:12.658
As a fellow warrior on the field
of battle, I will humbly accept it.

08:13.993 --> 08:16.954
Hey! Wait, Pyxis!

08:18.581 --> 08:21.334
Pyxis! Hey! Wait just a minute!

08:21.584 --> 08:23.878
I forbid you to leave!

08:24.754 --> 08:29.217
Assemble your troops immediately
and defend my domain!

08:29.967 --> 08:32.345
That is your duty!

08:35.139 --> 08:36.307
Lord Wald.

08:36.724 --> 08:41.479
As we speak, soldiers in Trost are
literally risking their lives in battle.

08:41.729 --> 08:44.148
Commander, I will prepare the horses.

08:45.107 --> 08:48.861
I presume many lives
are being lost as well.

08:49.195 --> 08:52.281
Right now, at this very moment.

08:52.448 --> 08:54.867
Insignificant lives, I'm sure.

08:54.951 --> 08:56.118
Forget about them.

08:56.869 --> 08:58.913
Your presence there
won't change anything anyway.

08:58.996 --> 09:03.960
You continually lose to me
in our tabletop skirmishes!

09:04.043 --> 09:06.003
Fear not, Your Lordship.

09:06.837 --> 09:09.173
Should he face the Titans
on a real battlefield,

09:09.465 --> 09:12.718
the Commander won't need to be
as lenient with them.

09:15.137 --> 09:16.347
Enough.

09:17.682 --> 09:18.766
Lord Wald.

09:19.308 --> 09:23.771
Please have another pleasant
and peaceful day as always.

09:26.649 --> 09:27.817
Hey.

09:28.943 --> 09:30.278
Pyxis!

09:30.361 --> 09:32.822
Come back! Pyxis!

09:33.239 --> 09:35.074
Pyxis!

09:37.910 --> 09:40.329
As practiced,
you will now split into your squads

09:40.538 --> 09:44.917
and perform resupply, message relay,
and Titan-clearing duties

09:45.001 --> 09:47.336
under the command
of the Garrison Regiment!

09:48.129 --> 09:50.590
The Garrison Regiment's
intercept squad will take the vanguard!

09:51.048 --> 09:53.884
The Cadet Corps, led by the support squad,
will take the middle guard!

09:54.135 --> 09:57.680
And the Garrison Regiment's
elite squads will take the rear guard!

09:58.097 --> 09:59.348
Additionally, I've received word

09:59.473 --> 10:02.393
that the advance team has been wiped out!

10:03.269 --> 10:06.814
The outer gate has been breached,
and the Titans have entered!

10:07.523 --> 10:11.944
In other words, the Armored Titan
could very well appear again

10:12.028 --> 10:14.739
and demolish the inner gate at any time!

10:16.365 --> 10:18.284
- You can't be serious.
- You've got to be kidding me.

10:19.118 --> 10:21.370
If they end up breaching Wall Rose too...

10:21.704 --> 10:22.872
Silence!

10:23.789 --> 10:25.958
The vanguard is currently engaged
with the enemy!

10:26.584 --> 10:28.878
This defense operation
has only one objective.

10:29.128 --> 10:33.507
To defend Wall Rose until the citizens
have finished evacuating!

10:34.258 --> 10:39.055
Also, as I'm sure you're well aware,
desertion is punishable by death!

10:39.513 --> 10:41.724
Be prepared to lay down your lives!

10:41.891 --> 10:42.850
Dismissed!

10:43.184 --> 10:44.060
- Sir!
- Sir!

10:49.815 --> 10:51.275
Why does it have to be today?

10:52.193 --> 10:54.153
I would have been on my way
to the interior tomorrow.

10:57.073 --> 10:58.032
Are you okay?

11:04.038 --> 11:07.750
No.

11:14.131 --> 11:15.049
Move!

11:16.050 --> 11:17.968
Hey, Jean! What's wrong?

11:18.094 --> 11:19.428
You're asking me what's wrong?

11:19.845 --> 11:22.973
That's easy for you to say,
you suicidal maniac!

11:23.182 --> 11:25.768
You want to join the Scouts!

11:25.893 --> 11:29.271
You're ready to be Titan chow anytime!

11:29.563 --> 11:31.774
I was headed for the interior tomorrow!

11:31.857 --> 11:32.775
Calm down!

11:32.858 --> 11:34.610
You expect me to calm down
and accept my death?

11:34.693 --> 11:35.528
No!

11:35.903 --> 11:36.946
Think back!

11:37.863 --> 11:40.366
Think back to the three years
of sweat and blood we endured!

11:41.867 --> 11:44.995
So many times we came close to dying
during those three years!

11:45.663 --> 11:47.164
Some people did die.

11:47.832 --> 11:50.251
Some ran off. Others were kicked out.

11:51.168 --> 11:52.753
But we survived!

11:53.212 --> 11:54.088
Right?

11:54.672 --> 11:57.007
I'm sure we can survive today too!

11:59.051 --> 12:02.847
You can just survive today
and leave for the interior tomorrow!

12:08.436 --> 12:09.270
Damn!

12:11.730 --> 12:14.650
Let's go, Daz! Quit your damn crying!

12:14.733 --> 12:16.277
Right.

12:17.111 --> 12:17.945
Eren.

12:19.155 --> 12:22.032
If the battle gets chaotic, come find me.

12:22.116 --> 12:24.910
What? We're in different squads!

12:25.619 --> 12:28.456
If the situation falls apart,
things won't go according to plan.

12:29.123 --> 12:30.583
I'll protect you!

12:30.749 --> 12:31.625
What the hell are--

12:31.709 --> 12:33.127
Cadet Ackermann.

12:34.170 --> 12:36.046
You're in the rearguard. Special orders.

12:36.213 --> 12:37.047
Come with me.

12:37.131 --> 12:39.925
I'm not skilled enough!
I'll only be a burden!

12:41.218 --> 12:43.429
I am not asking for your opinion.

12:44.013 --> 12:45.473
The citizens' evacuation is running late.

12:45.890 --> 12:48.642
We need as many elite soldiers
near them as possible.

12:49.059 --> 12:50.769
- But--
- Hey!

12:51.979 --> 12:53.522
Cut the crap, Mikasa!

12:54.106 --> 12:55.733
Quit freaking out like everyone else!

12:56.609 --> 12:58.444
Humanity is on the verge
of extinction here!

12:58.819 --> 13:01.405
This is no time to go and impose
your own selfish rules!

13:05.868 --> 13:09.246
I'm sorry. I wasn't thinking clearly.

13:11.790 --> 13:14.627
I do have one thing to ask.

13:17.630 --> 13:19.757
Please don't die.

13:27.056 --> 13:29.308
I'm not going to die.

13:30.518 --> 13:32.436
I can't die yet!

13:35.397 --> 13:39.401
Because I still don't know anything
about this world!

13:43.113 --> 13:48.160
Remaining historical documents say
nothing about the origin of the Titans.

13:48.661 --> 13:50.538
Most of the information
about them remains unknown.

13:51.413 --> 13:54.458
The things we do know about now,
including Titan ecology,

13:54.750 --> 13:57.795
are based entirely on the latest reports
from the Scout Regiment.

13:58.754 --> 14:02.550
We've been unable to determine if Titans
possess human-like intelligence.

14:02.800 --> 14:07.388
As such, there have been no cases
to date of mutual communication.

14:08.514 --> 14:12.935
Titan physiology is fundamentally
different from other living beings.

14:13.602 --> 14:17.523
They lack reproductive organs,
and it is unclear how they reproduce,

14:17.982 --> 14:20.609
but they primarily possess
male-like physiques.

14:21.485 --> 14:23.863
They have extremely high
body temperatures,

14:24.321 --> 14:25.698
and perplexingly enough, 

14:25.781 --> 14:29.201
 they show no interest
in any animals other than humans.

14:30.786 --> 14:34.290
Consuming people is
the Titans' sole principle of behavior,

14:34.707 --> 14:40.546
but given that they have existed for over
a century in a human-free environment,

14:41.213 --> 14:45.175
we can surmise that the very act
of feeding is unnecessary for them.

14:46.176 --> 14:50.306
In other words, it's believed that
they are not motivated by predation,

14:50.389 --> 14:51.724
but by bloodlust.

14:53.434 --> 14:57.605
And most of all, the Titans'
tremendous vitality is the primary reason

14:58.314 --> 15:01.025
that humankind has been
so greatly overwhelmed.

15:02.109 --> 15:05.446
Humanity has long possessed
cannon technology,

15:05.571 --> 15:07.740
but that alone wasn't enough
to combat them.

15:08.616 --> 15:11.201
Even when their heads are blown off,
the Titans don't die.

15:11.827 --> 15:13.495
Additionally, though times vary,

15:13.871 --> 15:17.333
their heads will fully regenerate
in only a minute or two.

15:17.708 --> 15:18.709
You can't be serious.

15:19.043 --> 15:20.961
Their size is bad enough as it is.

15:21.045 --> 15:23.964
Sir! Does that mean
the Titans are immortal?

15:25.591 --> 15:27.009
They are not immortal.

15:27.593 --> 15:29.553
There is one way to defeat a Titan.

15:30.804 --> 15:31.931
You target here.

15:33.015 --> 15:38.145
When severely damaged here,
a Titan will die without regenerating.

15:39.104 --> 15:42.900
That's where this pair
of flesh-paring blades comes in.

15:43.943 --> 15:46.695
A successful strike
to a Titan's weak spot with these

15:47.112 --> 15:51.200
will cause its immediate death,
with no time to regenerate whatsoever.

15:59.416 --> 16:00.376
Hey, Armin.

16:01.168 --> 16:03.212
This is the perfect chance,
don't you think?

16:04.797 --> 16:06.799
If we take care of business
in the first battle

16:07.591 --> 16:09.468
before we join the Scouts,

16:09.760 --> 16:13.514
we rookies will shoot up
the ranks for sure!

16:20.771 --> 16:22.940
Yes. No question about it.

16:23.565 --> 16:26.735
Just so you know,
you aren't the only ones in our class

16:26.819 --> 16:28.278
who want to join the Scouts.

16:28.737 --> 16:32.658
You beat us to the punch earlier,
but you won't outdo us this time!

16:32.783 --> 16:34.201
Sounds like a challenge, Thomas!

16:34.660 --> 16:37.287
Whoever takes out the most Titans wins!

16:37.997 --> 16:41.000
- Don't go messing with the scores!
- Squad 34, move out!

16:41.083 --> 16:42.668
Bolster the vanguard!

16:44.086 --> 16:45.504
All right! Let's go!

16:45.754 --> 16:47.131
- Yes!
- Yes!

17:09.945 --> 17:11.321
So many Titans already?

17:11.947 --> 17:14.033
The vanguard has been totally routed!

17:14.366 --> 17:17.578
What are they doing?
Those hot shots usually act all tough!

17:18.579 --> 17:22.791
I figured things would be bad,
but not like this!

17:24.043 --> 17:25.169
An Abnormal!

17:26.045 --> 17:27.004
Stop!

17:44.313 --> 17:45.189
What?

18:10.380 --> 18:12.132
What the hell are you doing?

18:12.800 --> 18:15.260
- Eren!
- Don't go off on your own!

18:18.847 --> 18:20.265
Get back here, damn it!

18:21.600 --> 18:23.435
You're going to pay for killing Thomas!

18:23.977 --> 18:27.064
I won't let you get away!

18:38.325 --> 18:39.201
Eren!

18:39.785 --> 18:40.702
Eren!

18:57.511 --> 19:00.055
Stop! Please don't!

19:06.937 --> 19:09.398
Why am I...

19:10.274 --> 19:13.986
Why am I watching as my friends get eaten?

19:21.326 --> 19:26.248
Why can't I move?

19:37.092 --> 19:38.969
Armin.

19:40.846 --> 19:43.348
Eren!

19:44.057 --> 19:44.975
Eren!

19:46.977 --> 19:48.270
What is it, Armin?

19:48.395 --> 19:51.440
My grandpa was secretly keeping this!

19:51.815 --> 19:54.443
It's a book about the outside world!

19:55.194 --> 19:57.321
A book about the outside world?

19:57.821 --> 19:59.698
Isn't it illegal to have those?

20:00.407 --> 20:01.742
You're going to get arrested!

20:01.825 --> 20:04.620
This is no time to be saying that!

20:04.786 --> 20:05.954
According to this book,

20:06.038 --> 20:09.917
most of the world is covered
in a body of water called "sea"!

20:10.167 --> 20:12.920
And this "sea" is entirely saltwater!

20:13.003 --> 20:14.046
Salt?

20:14.546 --> 20:17.716
You're lying! Salt is so precious!

20:17.925 --> 20:20.302
I'm sure merchants
would have snatched it all up!

20:20.385 --> 20:23.222
You can't though! The sea is that big!

20:23.305 --> 20:24.723
As if.

20:25.557 --> 20:28.018
There's a lot more than loads of salt too!

20:28.268 --> 20:32.314
Fiery water! Lands of ice!
Sandy snowfields!

20:32.731 --> 20:35.067
The outside world
must be many times larger than

20:35.150 --> 20:36.818
the inside of these walls!

20:37.819 --> 20:39.738
The outside world...

20:40.322 --> 20:42.950
And this is still a secret,

20:43.700 --> 20:47.746
but my mom and dad are planning
to venture into the outside world!

20:48.747 --> 20:50.624
The outside world...

20:51.124 --> 20:52.376
Hey, Eren.

20:53.168 --> 20:57.130
I hope we can explore
the outside world too someday!

21:16.775 --> 21:17.693
Eren!

21:19.194 --> 21:22.447
I refuse to die here.

21:25.450 --> 21:27.703
Listen, Armin.

21:29.079 --> 21:32.457
You told me about it.

21:33.625 --> 21:37.045
So I have to see it.

21:37.629 --> 21:38.964
The outside world!

21:41.842 --> 21:42.759
Eren!

21:43.093 --> 21:44.052
Hurry!

23:43.421 --> 23:45.215
Suddenly, it begins to rain.

23:45.841 --> 23:47.551
The quiet sound of rainfall,

23:47.884 --> 23:52.472
the damp air,
and the faintly sweet smell of rain...

23:52.764 --> 23:55.809
They remind Mikasa
of a ghastly incident from her past.
